From f3801aafc91b0a1a10aaf283be2bfe120c16d568 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Lenin Aviles <lenin.aviles@hearst.com>
Date: Mon, 21 Sep 2026 17:56:06 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] fix(tailwind): correct dangling token reference in
 scrollbar-dark
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

var(--colors-neutral-4) is plural and was never defined; the token is
--color-neutral-4. Both declarations in @utility scrollbar-dark were inert,
so the dark scrollbar thumb had no colour at all.

Also fixes the adjacent -webskit-scrollbar typo in the same block.

Now covered by rule ST-01, which scans var() references across the whole
stylesheet rather than only token declarations — this defect lives inside an
@utility block, where a declarations-only scan would never have found it.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/tailwind/ids.css | 6 +++---
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/tailwind/ids.css b/src/tailwind/ids.css
index b39c484..3dd6830 100644
--- a/src/tailwind/ids.css
+++ b/src/tailwind/ids.css
@@ -250,18 +250,18 @@
 }
 
 @utility scrollbar-dark {
-  &::-webskit-scrollbar {
+  &::-webkit-scrollbar {
     cursor: default !important;
     width: 6px;
   }
   &::-webkit-scrollbar-thumb {
-    background-color: var(--colors-neutral-4);
+    background-color: var(--color-neutral-4);
     border-radius: 8px;
   }
   &::-webkit-scrollbar-track {
     background: transparent;
   }
-  scrollbar-color: var(--colors-neutral-4);
+  scrollbar-color: var(--color-neutral-4);
   scrollbar-width: thin;
 }
 
